    {
      "id": "s03",
      "type": "UV_STAGE",
      "narration": "Welcome back to THE NBX STUDIO, where we take one tool and actually use it — follow along if that is your kind of thing. If you write Python, you already know the drill. pip installs your packages. virtualenv keeps them apart. pyenv juggles interpreters. pipx handles command-line tools, and poetry tries to hold the whole thing together. Five tools, five ways to get it wrong. uv is a single binary that covers all five, and today we're taking it from an empty folder to a package you could publish. So where does that actually save you time?",
